   ],
   "example": [
    "“Gradiresti un caffè? - Non a quest'ora.”",
    "word for word: Would-you-like a coffee? - Not at this-hour.",
    "— Benvenuti al Sud (2010), 0:26:14"
   ],
   "italian": "il caffè",
   "english": "coffee",
   "hint": "",
   "details": "masculine · plural: i caffè",
   "forms": "",
   "ipa": "/kafˈfɛ/",
   "note": "Invariable: due caffè. Also means a café.",
   "fact": "Order 'un caffè' in Italy and you get an espresso. Ask for a long milky coffee with a caffè latte. The word came via Ottoman Turkish kahve from Arabic qahwa.",
