  {
   "slug": "la-fine",
   "deck": "italian_cils_a2",
   "recognition": true,
   "production": true,
   "pills": [
    "noun"
   ],
   "example": [
    "“Passa un buon fine settimana.”",
    "word for word: Spend a good end week.",
    "— Benvenuti al Sud (2010), 0:51:35"
   ],
   "italian": "la fine",
   "english": "end",
   "hint": "conclusion",
   "details": "feminine",
   "forms": "",
   "ipa": "/ˈfi.ne/",
   "note": "Alla fine = in the end. Il fine settimana = weekend. Il fine (masculine) = aim, purpose.",
   "fact": "The gender changes the meaning: la fine is the end or conclusion, il fine is the aim or purpose. 'Il fine giustifica i mezzi' means 'the end justifies the means'.",
   "facttitle": "Usage"
  },
  {
