  },
  {
   "slug": "la-grazia",
   "deck": "italian_frequency",
   "recognition": true,
   "production": true,
   "pills": [
    "noun"
   ],
   "example": [
    "“Venendo? - No, grazie, non ho fame.”",
    "word for word: Coming? - No, thanks, not I-have hunger.",
    "— Benvenuti al Sud (2010), 0:37:15"
   ],
   "italian": "la grazia",
   "english": "grace",
   "hint": "",
   "details": "feminine",
   "forms": "",
   "ipa": "/ˈɡrat.sja/",
   "note": "The plural grazie also means 'thank you'.",
   "fact": "Grazie (thank you) is just the plural of this word: literally 'graces, favours', from Latin gratias agere (to give thanks). English grace and gratitude share the root.",
   "facttitle": "Did you know?"
  },
  {
   "slug": "questo",
   "deck": "italian_movies_benvenuti_al_sud",
   "recognition": true,
   "production": false,
   "pills": [
